  "diagnosis_text": "Diagnosis: **the configured s3\u2013s1 link is down, while s3 still forwards h5 traffic toward that link.**\n\nEvidence:\n\n- `h1 \u2192 h5`: 100% packet loss.\n- `h1 \u2192 h6`: also 100% loss, so this is not isolated to h5\u2019s host port.\n- `h1 \u2192 h2`: succeeds locally on s3, confirming h1 and its s3 access port work.\n- `h3 \u2192 h5`: succeeds, confirming h5 and s5 remain reachable from elsewhere.\n- The configured link is **s3 port 1 \u2194 s1 port 2**, but:\n  - both ports report `enabled: false`;\n  - the link is absent from ONOS\u2019s active-link list.\n- s3\u2019s flow for h5\u2019s MAC (`00:00:00:00:00:05`) outputs to **port 1**. Its packet counter increased, showing traffic is being sent toward the disabled port.\n\n**Localisation:** s3 port 1 / s1 port 2, or the link between them. ONOS forwarding has not rerouted h1\u2019s traffic over the available s3\u2013s2 or s3\u2013s4 paths.\n\nNext step: investigate why those two ports are disabled, then restore the link or update/reinstall the baseline forwarding rules to use an active path.",
